# This tool's worker image, named by a local deep-deps mount: the path is
# relative to THIS directory, and the root `.caos-expr` deepens the repo, so
# `DEEP-DEPS/nim` exists in the tree this directory's `.caos-expr` is evaluated
# against (caos design/caos-expr.md).
#
# caos/nim rather than caos's std/bash, and that is load-bearing rather than a
# convenience: every one of these tools compiles Nim, and the test batches MUST
# run on this image — the test binary hardcodes the ELF interpreter of the glibc
# it was linked against, which is the one in here. caos/nim satisfies everything
# std/bash would have: bash, coreutils, and the same /worker trampoline that
# runs `worker1`.
../../caos/nim nim
